WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.957
Some Transformer tokens are control symbols rather than ordinary words.

00:00:04.957 --> 00:00:10.447
In many BERT-style models, C L S can be placed at the beginning of a sequence and can

00:00:10.447 --> 00:00:14.787
support sequence-level tasks such as classification.

00:00:14.787 --> 00:00:18.672
S E P can mark a boundary between segments.

00:00:18.672 --> 00:00:25.902
P A D fills shorter examples so that several sequences can be placed in one rectangular batch.

00:00:25.902 --> 00:00:29.997
M A S K is used in masked-language-model training and in fill-mask demonstrations.

00:00:29.997 --> 00:00:32.622
These conventions are model-specific.

00:00:32.622 --> 00:00:39.157
A decoder-only model may use different beginning-of-sequence, end-of-sequence, or padding rules.

00:00:39.157 --> 00:00:48.022
The safest approach is to let the tokenizer add and manage the special tokens for the chosen checkpoint.

00:00:48.022 --> 00:00:53.537
If you manually add the wrong symbols or use conventions from another model family,

00:00:53.537 --> 00:00:56.835
the input may not match what the model saw during training.
